.TH AGENT-HOOK-COMPACT 1 "2026-10-13" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-hook-compact \- record that an agent is about to compact its context
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-hook-compact
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-hook-compact
handles the
.B PreCompact
lifecycle event. It reads the hook JSON payload from standard input and runs
.BR "hm hook context-reset" ,
so Hive Memory stops treating earlier injected memories as visible and offers
them again after compaction. It does so only for runtimes whose Hive Memory
delivery tracking needs it (Claude Code and Codex); elsewhere it does nothing.
Muse keeps session-start context through compaction and drops prompt context
every turn, so its compaction loses nothing and needs no reset.
.PP
If the reset fails, the hook leaves a marker in the session state directory and
the next
.BR agent-hook-prompt-submit (1)
asks for the reset again. The response is always empty JSON; a failure is
reported on standard error and in telemetry only.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_HIVE_MEMORY_HOOKS
Set to
.B 0
to disable Hive Memory hook integration.
.TP
.B AGENTGUARD_HIVE_MEMORY_DELIVERY
Set to
.BR 0 ,
.BR false ,
.BR no ,
or
.B off
to keep every runtime on untracked Hive Memory hooks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Always; compaction is never blocked.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-hook-prompt-submit (1),
.BR agent-hook-session-start (1),
.BR hm (1)
